                    \\,.
            %p Moreover:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear dependence
                  on the tangent vector) these differentials are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
                  with respect to the vector space structure on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+spaces"} tangent spaces
                  from lemma
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearTangentSpace"}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable dependence
                  on the base point) globally they yield a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  of real
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+vector+bundles"} differentiable vector bundles
                  between the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
                  (def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentBundle"}
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiableTangentBundle"}
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi T
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d f \;\colon\; T X \longrightarrow T Y
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+rule"}> chain rule
                  ) The assignment
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi d
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \mapsto d f
                  respects
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  in that for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                  three
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
                  and for
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi A
                            %mi f
                            %mphantom
                              %mi A
                        %mi Y
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi A
                            %mi g
                            %mphantom
                              %mi A
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X
                        \\overset{\phantom{A}f\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}
                        Y
                        \\overset{\phantom{A}g\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}
                        Z
                %p
                  two
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+functions"} differentiable functions
                  then their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
                  satisfy
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d(g \circ f) = (d g) \circ (d f)
                        \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              All statements are to be tested on charts of an atlas for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanSpaceTangentBundle"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (tangent
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %p
              In the language of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              the statement of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctionsBetweenDifferentiableManifoldsDifferentials"}
              says that forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+functions"} differentiable functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \;\colon\; Diff \longrightarrow Vect(Diff)
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
              to the category of differentiable real vector bundles.
          #VectorField.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"}> vector field
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
              with differentiable tangent bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \to X
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TangentBundle"}
            %p
              A differentiable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \colon X \to T X
              of the tangent bundle is called a (differentiable)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong (notation for tangent vectors in a chart)
            %p
              Under the bijection of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearTangentSpace"}
              one often denotes the tangent vector corresponding to the the
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} basis
              vector of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mtext or just
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{\partial}{\partial x^i}
                    \\phantom{AA} \text{or just } \phantom{AA}
                    \\partial_i
            %p
              because under the identification of tangent vectors with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
              on the algebra of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+functions"} differentiable functions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as
              %a{:href => "#AlgebraicDefinition"} above
              then it acts as the operation of taking the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \mathbb{R}^n
              is then denoted by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mtext or just
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{n}{\sum}
                    v^i
                    \\frac{\partial}{\partial x^i}
                    \\phantom{AA} \text{or just } \phantom{AA}
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{n}{\sum} v^i \partial_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that this identification depends on the choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
            %p
              Sometimes, notably in texts on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermodynamics"} thermodynamics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
              on a 2-dimensional manifold are used as coordinate functions for a local chart (i.e. so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^1 = f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = g
              ), then one writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
