            %p
              The linearity of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+rule"} product rule
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
              imply that this function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_v
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              on the algebra of smooth functions. Hence there is a function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
