                        \\stackrel{\bar v}{\to} X)
                  ,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar v
                  is the hom-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          %p
            This definition captures elegantly and usefully the notion of tangent vectors as infinitesimal curves. But it is not guaranteed that the fibers of a synthetic tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D
            are fiberwise linear, i.e. are fiberwise
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for which this is true are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microlinear+space"} microlinear spaces
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            is called a
            %em well-adapted model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            embedding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{T}
            of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifolds
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          %p Typically, for well adapted models, under this embedding
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                manifolds are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microlinear+space"} microlinear spaces
            %li
              %p
                the synthetic definition of tangent bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^D
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a manifold does coincide with the ordinary notion of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi fin
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L} = (C^\infty Ring^{fin})^{op}
            be the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} smooth loci
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^D
            does exist in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}
            and is isomorphic to the ordinary tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Models+for+Smooth+Infinitesimal+Analysis"} MSIA, chapter II, prop 1.12
          %p
            There are well-adapted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topoi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒵
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Z}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            presented as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} categories of sheaves
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            where covers are
            %em finite
            open covers, the second where covers are finite open covers and projections (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Models+for+Smooth+Infinitesimal+Analysis"}> MSIA, chapter VI
            ). Both topologies are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y : \mathbb{L} \to Sh(\mathbb{L})
            does preserve the above property.
          %p
            Hence in these models for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Diff
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \in Diff
            its ordinary tangent bundle and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : Diff \to Sh(\mathbb{L})
            the full and faithful embedding, we have isomorphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi D
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (s(X))^D  \simeq s(T X)
          %p which respect the bundle maps.
          %h3#in_supergeometry In supergeometry
          %p
            The tangent bundle of a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be interpreted as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and the tangent vectors have degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+tangent+bundle"} shifted tangent bundle
          %h3#for_other_generalized_smooth_spaces For other generalized smooth spaces
          %p
            There are useful categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth spaces
            which are neither categories of manifolds nor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+topos"} smooth topoi
            modeling
